 "voice": [
  {
   "id": "vo01",
   "t": 0.1,
   "dur": 4.789,
   "file": "vo/01.wav",
   "text": "Why is this cell folded? Because the road ahead is narrower than the cell."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo02",
   "t": 5.9,
   "dur": 10.349,
   "file": "vo/02.wav",
   "text": "Meet a red blood cell: a disc about seven micrometers across, dimpled on both sides, with no nucleus. You have about twenty-five trillion of them: most of your own cells."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo03",
   "t": 17.1,
   "dur": 9.072,
   "file": "vo/03.wav",
   "text": "Now follow it as the vessel branches, and branches again, into a capillary. The narrowest are slimmer than the cell, so cells go through in single file."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo04",
   "t": 27.1,
   "dur": 8.79,
   "file": "vo/04.wav",
   "text": "Here's the trick. The dimples give it spare surface for its volume, so it can fold into a parachute without stretching. Squeeze, slide, spring back."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo05",
   "t": 38.7,
   "dur": 8.858,
   "file": "vo/05.wav",
   "text": "The tightest are about three micrometers: less than half its width. And it squeezes through them for its whole life: about a hundred and twenty days."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo06",
   "t": 51.5,
   "dur": 6.333,
   "file": "vo/06.wav",
   "text": "So that dimple isn't decoration. It gets your blood through your smallest vessels, where oxygen is handed out."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo07",
   "t": 58.7,
   "dur": 5.093,
   "file": "vo/07.wav",
   "text": "Meanwhile, as you watched, your bone marrow made over a hundred million new red cells."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo08",
   "t": 64.7,
   "dur": 4.08,
   "file": "vo/08.wav",
   "text": "Next time: what this cell is carrying. About a billion passengers."
  }
 ]
}